  "preamble": "Deaffrication of the lateral affricate [tɬ] to [t] is characteristic of the eastern periphery of Nahuan: Pipil and Highland Puebla Nahuatl have t where Classical Nahuatl has tl, both in roots (metlatl vs. metat 'metate') and in the absolutive suffix -tl > -t (cōlōtl vs. kulut 'scorpion').",
  "phoneticEffects": "Deaffrication",
